<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Hookmark 7.3 is out, and Luc Beaudoin and his team keep adding to what was already one of the cleverer utilities on the Mac.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If you haven&#8217;t run into it, <a href="https://hookproductivity.com">Hookmark links your stuff together across apps</a>. Hook a PDF in DEVONthink to the OmniFocus project it belongs to, or an email to the Obsidian note where you&#8217;re drafting the reply, and you can jump between them from either side. The links run both directions, and they work between apps that otherwise know nothing about each other.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The feature I&#8217;d point to first is Clean My Links. When you copy or hook a web link, Hookmark strips out the tracking parameters and other junk that turns a simple URL into a paragraph. It doesn&#8217;t route anything through a link-shortening service or change the domain. You get the short, readable link the page should have had in the first place. It&#8217;s on by default, and 7.3 makes it better.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Luc has also been open about where Hookmark is headed. The team says it&#8217;s working on Apple Intelligence support so you can ask questions about the network of links you&#8217;ve built. Congratulations to team Hookmark for <a href="https://hookproductivity.com">the latest release.</a></p>
